    <h2 id="contribute">Contributing</h2>
    <p>Research questions and new models are welcome in design issues. New theorems in existing chapters, documentation, and applications built on the existing layers can go straight to a pull request. Small, well-scoped additions to the <code>ForMathlib</code> folder can be suitable first contributions.</p>
    <p>Changes to the foundational layers start with a design issue: sketch the definitions and main statements and get agreement on the shape before writing proofs. Every pull request must build cleanly, contain no <code>sorry</code>, <code>admit</code>, or <code>native_decide</code>, and add no axioms beyond the standard three.</p>
    <p>Lean contributors should read <a href="{{ site.repository }}/blob/{{ site.sourceBranch }}/CONTRIBUTING.md">CONTRIBUTING.md</a> for the build, API, and review requirements. New contributors can work through the beginner's manual, improve documentation, or discuss a small task in <a href="{{ site.issues }}">GitHub Issues</a>. PRs touching the core layers require a maintainer review before merge.</p>
    <p>For a first contribution, try <a href="{{ site.issues }}/118">documenting the BidderProblem umbrella</a>, a small documentation task with a starting file and build instructions.</p>
    <h3>Propose a focused research project</h3>
    <p>Email <a href="mailto:contact@mathecon.dev">contact@mathecon.dev</a> or open a design issue. Describe the economic question and relevant literature, the intended definitions and assumptions, the main statement or example to formalize, and the existing library components you expect to reuse. Identify any changes to foundational definitions so the team can agree on the design before proofs are written.</p>

